---
import BaseLayout from "../../../components/layout/BaseLayout.astro";
import MetaPill from "../../../components/ui/MetaPill.astro";
import registry from "../../../data/phase-83-community-institutions-social-infrastructure-collective-resilience-registry.json";

const institutions = registry.community_institution_access_trust_continuity_dossiers;
const civic = registry.civic_association_cooperative_mutual_aid_capacity_ledgers;
const information = registry.local_information_media_public_knowledge_integrity_registers;
const resilience = registry.collective_preparedness_trauma_recovery_resilience_ledgers;
---

<BaseLayout title="Community Institutions And Collective Resilience | FTFN" description="Thirty-two inactive community-institution, civic-network, local-information, and collective-resilience records.">
  <section class="page-section hero" data-community-institutions-registry><div class="hero__copy"><div class="eyebrow">FTFN / Community Institutions</div><h1 class="page-title">Institution presence is not community access, and reopening is not collective recovery.</h1><p class="lede">Phase 83 traces whether households can rely on trusted local institutions, inclusive civic networks, mutual-aid capacity, public-interest information, accessible community hubs, democratic preparedness, collective repair, and durable resilience.</p><div class="meta-row"><MetaPill label="8 inactive institution dossiers" tone="possibility" /><MetaPill label="8 inactive civic ledgers" /><MetaPill label="8 inactive information registers" /><MetaPill label="8 inactive resilience ledgers" /><MetaPill label="0 community decisions" tone="review" /></div></div></section>

  <section class="page-section"><div class="section-heading"><div><div class="eyebrow">Institutions, Access And Trust</div><h2>Eight community-institution dossiers remain closed.</h2></div><a class="inline-link" href="/briefings/community-institutions-doctrine-001/">Read the institution doctrine</a></div><div class="grid">{institutions.map((record) => <article class="record-card"><div class="meta-row"><MetaPill label={record.institution_state} tone="review" /><MetaPill label="20 inactive gates" /></div><h3><a href={'/evidence/community-institutions/' + record.slug + '/'}>{record.named_entity}</a></h3><p>Institution purpose, ownership, access, trust, workforce, funding, assets, referrals, continuity, closure, displacement, distribution, remedy, review, and receipts remain empty.</p></article>)}</div></section>

  <section class="page-section"><div class="section-heading"><div><div class="eyebrow">Civic Networks, Cooperatives And Mutual Aid</div><h2>Eight civic-capacity ledgers contain no finding.</h2></div><a class="inline-link" href="/briefings/mutual-aid-volunteer-capacity-001/">Read the mutual-aid guide</a></div><div class="grid">{civic.map((record) => <article class="record-card"><div class="meta-row"><MetaPill label={record.civic_state} tone="review" /><MetaPill label="20 inactive gates" /></div><h3><a href={'/evidence/community-institutions/' + record.slug + '/'}>{record.civic_association_cooperative_mutual_aid_capacity_ledger_id}: {record.named_entity}</a></h3><p>Membership, governance, ownership, cooperative capacity, mutual-aid demand and offers, volunteers, paid work, training, resources, surge, succession, conflicts, and fallback remain unassessed.</p></article>)}</div></section>

  <section class="page-section"><div class="section-heading"><div><div class="eyebrow">Local Information And Public Knowledge</div><h2>Eight information-integrity registers remain inactive.</h2></div><a class="inline-link" href="/briefings/local-media-information-integrity-001/">Read the local-information guide</a></div><div class="source-list">{information.map((record) => <article class="source-row"><div><h3><a href={'/evidence/community-institutions/' + record.slug + '/'}>{record.local_information_media_public_knowledge_integrity_register_id}: {record.named_entity}</a></h3><p>Information need, reporting, public records, ownership, funding, accessibility, community knowledge, provenance, correction, distribution, safety, trusted intermediaries, public reason, and review remain unassessed.</p></div><MetaPill label={record.information_state} tone="review" /></article>)}</div></section>

  <section class="page-section"><div class="section-heading"><div><div class="eyebrow">Preparedness, Trauma, Recovery And Resilience</div><h2>Eight collective-resilience ledgers contain no activation.</h2></div><a class="inline-link" href="/briefings/collective-trauma-recovery-001/">Read the collective-recovery guide</a></div><div class="grid">{resilience.map((record) => <article class="record-card"><h3><a href={'/evidence/community-institutions/' + record.slug + '/'}>{record.collective_preparedness_trauma_recovery_resilience_ledger_id}: {record.named_entity}</a></h3><p>Risk, hubs, warnings, essential continuity, mutual aid, trauma support, cultural continuity, institution closure, displacement, reconstruction, public-space restoration, reconnection, normalization, learning, and audit remain inactive.</p><MetaPill label={record.resilience_state} tone="review" /></article>)}</div></section>

  <section class="page-section briefing-band"><div class="briefing-band__copy"><div class="eyebrow">Public Contract</div><h2>Inspect the empty community-capacity state.</h2><p>The export publishes the complete control surface without admitting an institution or network, assigning volunteers or funds, classifying truth, suppressing content, activating an emergency, closing or restoring an institution, declaring recovery, or creating a receipt, score, rank, or stage change.</p></div><article class="record-card"><a class="inline-link" href="/data/community-institutions-social-infrastructure-collective-resilience.json">Community institutions JSON</a></article></section>
</BaseLayout>
